,m}:M_n→M_m for n≥m.","fixed_by":"def-inverse-system-and-inverse-limit-of-modules","matters_for":["thm-universal-property-of-an-inverse-limit-of-modules","thm-inverse-limits-are-left-exact","def-mittag-leffler-inverse-system","def-separated-and-complete-filtered-module","def-adic-completion-of-a-module"]},{"convention":"A filtered module is complete only when it is separated and its canonical map to the quotient inverse limit is an isomorphism.","fixed_by":"def-separated-and-complete-filtered-module","matters_for":["thm-kernel-and-universal-property-of-adic-completion","thm-finite-modules-over-complete-noetherian-rings-are-complete","thm-complete-nakayama-lemma"]},{"convention":"Projective resolutions are augmented exact chain complexes in nonnegative homological degrees; syzygies are relative to the displayed resolution.","fixed_by":"def-projective-resolution-in-an-abelian-category","matters_for":["def-length-of-a-resolution","def-syzygy-and-cosyzygy-relative-to-a-resolution","thm-projective-comparison-map-exists","thm-horseshoe-lemma-for-projective-resolutions","thm-schanuel-lemma-in-an-abelian-category"]},{"convention":"The projective comparison-map existence and uniqueness proofs explicitly assume Dependent Choice for their countable successor-by-successor choices.","fixed_by":"thm-projective-comparison-map-exists","matters_for":["thm-projective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-chain-homotopy","thm-projective-resolutions-of-the-same-object-are-homotopy-equivalent-over-that-object","thm-injective-comparison-map-exists","thm-injective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-cochain-homotopy"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"def-rees-algebra-and-rees-module","statement":"Defines the Rees algebra and Rees module, and additionally asserts for the I-adic filtration that R(M_•)/tR(M_•) is naturally gr_I(M).","used_by":["lem-rees-module-finiteness-and-stable-filtrations","thm-artin-rees-lemma"]},{"id":"thm-hilbert-serre-theorem","statement":"For a finite graded module over S=A[x_1,…,