-tensor-products","used_for":"tensor and local-flatness arguments","opened":true},{"id":"thm-universal-property-of-module-tensor-products","used_for":"tensor-product references","opened":true},{"id":"thm-zorn","used_for":"generator extension detects injectivity","opened":true}],"concerns":[{"id":"def-graded-ring-and-graded-module","concern":"The final sentence says that the positive-degree part is generated as an S_0-algebra. The positive-degree part generally has no unit and is not an S_0-algebra; standard graded should say that S itself is generated as an S_0-algebra by degree-one elements.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-hilbert-function-and-hilbert-series","concern":"With M indexed over all of Z and no bounded-below hypothesis, the displayed bilateral sum need not be a formal Laurent series: it can have infinitely many negative powers.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-rees-algebra-and-rees-module","concern":"For the I-adic filtration, t is generally not an element of R(I), and tR(M_•) need not be contained in R(M_•). Thus the displayed quotient R(M_•)/tR(M_•) is generally undefined; it cannot supply gr_I(M) as written.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-inverse-system-and-inverse-limit-of-modules","concern":"The transition maps are called arrows of R-modules but are never required to be R-linear. Without that, compatible tuples need not form the asserted submodule.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-hilbert-serre-theorem","concern":"Step 1.4 invokes the theorem for the r−1-variable algebra as an “algebra hypothesis,” but no induction hypothesis is stated. The usual induction is short, but it is absent from the written proof.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-faithful-flatness-detected-by-nonzero-modules-and-fibres","concern":"Step 1.1 calls the unique morphism 0→N nonzero. It is always the zero morphism, so that stated contradiction does not prove 1⇒2. The conclusion follows instead by reflecting exactness of the full zero complex.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-injective-comparison-map-exists","concern":"The proof imports thm-projective-comparison-map-exists through the opposite category. That cited theorem explicitly assumes Dependent Choice, but this theorem has no such hypothesis.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-injective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-cochain-homotopy","concern":"The proof dualizes thm-projective-comparison-maps-are-unique-up-to-chain-homotopy, whose statement explicitly assumes Dependent Choice, but the injective theorem omits that assumption.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"lem-transfinite-iteration-of-the-generator-extension-preserves-monomorphisms-and-factorizes-small-source-maps","concern":"Step 3.1 asserts that every map N→colim_{α<λ}M_α from N⊆U factors through an earlier stage merely from a cofinality bound on indexing data. Such factorization requires a smallness/presentability condition on N relative to the filtered colimit, which is neither assumed nor proved; cardinality of subobjects and maps is insufficient.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"cor-flat-quotients-and-idempotent-ideals","concern":"[L2] states that local rings have only trivial idempotents without the Axiom-of-Choice hypothesis carried by the cited corollary. The item adds no AC assumption.","severity":"would-be-fatal"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}